    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty tough reality to face. If we are looking at it from a purely data-driven standpoint for the NGO, does that mean we should basically deprioritize minority-led or lower-income districts in future disaster models to avoid that \"dependency\" you mentioned? \n\nBasically, if we want to maximize our \"success rate,\" is it more logical to statistically favor areas that are already white or high-income since they have a higher probability of a successful outcome?",
